/**
@page limits Limits

BONet supports a bounded number of each stacked element, set by compile-time
constants. Override one by defining it before the backend header:

@code{.c}
#define BNT_MAX_VLAN_DEPTH 4
#include "bnt_xdp.h"
@endcode

| Constant                  | Default | Maximum                |
| ------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- |
| @c BNT_MAX_VLAN_DEPTH     | 2       | VLAN tags              |
| @c BNT_MAX_IPV6_EXT_DEPTH | 6       | IPv6 extension headers |
| @c BNT_SRV6_MAX_SEGS      | 8       | SRH segments           |

A stack deeper than its bound returns @c BNT_ERR_TOO_DEEP. Raising a bound covers
deeper stacks at the cost of more verifier instructions; lowering one is cheaper
but rejects deeper packets.
*/
